    "sha": "047299f1f890b7bc3c658c7608b4de6623efc0b9",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOQ337w9oAKDA0NzI5OWYxZjg5MGI3YmMzYzY1OGM3NjA4YjRkZTY2MjNlZmMwYjk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Debanjan Maji",
        "email": "debanjanmaji700@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-12T17:16:00Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Debanjan Maji",
        "email": "debanjanmaji700@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-02-12T17:16:00Z"
      },
      "message": "fix: add missing sign_extend property to instructions with signed immediates\n\nMany instruction YAML files define variables for immediates that are sign-extended when used in the operation (indicated by \\\\(imm)\\), but the encoding section does not include the \\sign_extend: true\\ property.\n\nThis PR adds \\sign_extend: true\\ to 29 instruction YAML files across I, C, F, and Zfh extensions where the immediate is used with \\\\(imm)\\ directly in the operation.\n\nNote: Prefetch instructions (prefetch.i/r/w) are NOT included because they apply sign extension after a shift operation (\\\\(imm << 5)\\), not at extraction time. Adding \\sign_extend: true\\ to these would be incorrect.\n\nFixes #1299",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "0a6d100d9da9a52871565cabc461a114c2c1bbd2",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-unified-db/git/trees/0a6d100d9da9a52871565cabc461a114c2c1bbd2"
